# Stripe restricted, READ-ONLY API key.
# Create in Stripe dashboard: Developers -> API keys -> Restricted keys.
# Scope read-only: Payouts (read), Subscriptions (read), Customers (read),
# Balance transactions (read). Live mode (sk_live_.../rk_live_...) for real data.
# Never commit the real key: this file only documents the variable name.
STRIPE_API_KEY=

# --- Multi-account (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# This server can talk to up to three SEPARATE Stripe accounts (NOT Connect
# sub-accounts), so each needs its own restricted read-only key. Give each the
# same 8 Read scopes: Payouts, Subscriptions, Customers, Balance,
# Balance Transaction Sources, Products, Prices, Invoices.
#
#   STRIPE_API_KEY            -> the "primary" account   [the default]
#   STRIPE_API_KEY_SECOND     -> the "second" account
#   STRIPE_API_KEY_THIRD      -> the "third" account
#
# Leave the extra two blank if you only use one account. To label the accounts
# in tool output, set the matching *_LABEL and *_ACCT variables.
STRIPE_API_KEY_SECOND=
STRIPE_API_KEY_THIRD=

# Optional display labels and account ids (acct_...) shown in tool descriptions.
STRIPE_LABEL_PRIMARY=Primary
STRIPE_LABEL_SECOND=Second
STRIPE_LABEL_THIRD=Third
STRIPE_ACCT_PRIMARY=
STRIPE_ACCT_SECOND=
STRIPE_ACCT_THIRD=
